     the converse membership relation (which is not an equivalence relation)
     leaves a set unchanged.  See also ~ dfcnqs .

     _Note:  This is the last lemma (from which the axioms will be derived) in_
     _the construction of real and complex numbers.  The construction starts_
     _at_ ~ cnpi .  (Contributed by NM, 13-Aug-1995.)
     (New usage is discouraged.) $)
  mulcnsrec $p |- ( ( ( A e. R. /\ B e. R. ) /\ ( C e. R. /\ D e. R. ) ) ->
               ( [ <. A , B >. ] `' _E x. [ <. C , D >. ] `' _E ) =
                    [ <. ( ( A .R C ) +R ( -1R .R ( B .R D ) ) ) ,
