       For example, ` ( sqrt `` 2 5 ) = 5 ` ( ~ ex-sqrt ).

       Since ` ( y ^ 2 ) = x ` iff ` ( -u y ^ 2 ) = x ` , we ensure uniqueness
       by restricting the range to numbers with positive real part, or numbers
       with 0 real part and nonnegative imaginary part.  A description can be
       found under "Principal square root of a complex number" at
       ~ http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Square_root .  The square root symbol was
       introduced in 1525 by Christoff Rudolff.

