  ${
    $d g k m n x $.
    $( Define the Bernoulli polynomials.  Here we use well-founded recursion to
       define the Bernoulli polynomials.  This agrees with most textbook
       definitions, although explicit formulas do exist.  (Contributed by Scott
       Fenton, 22-May-2014.) $)
    df-bpoly $a |- BernPoly =
       ( m e. NN0 , x e. CC |->
         ( wrecs ( < , NN0 , ( g e. _V |-> [_ ( # ` dom g ) / n ]_
            ( ( x ^ n ) - sum_ k e. dom g ( ( n _C k ) x.
              ( ( g ` k ) / ( ( n - k )
              + 1 ) ) ) ) ) ) ` m ) ) $.
  $}

